>
>I did something like that once and saw my character dying of hunger
>without being able to do anything for him ...

What I do in this situation is to type "99." repeatedly.  This method
guarantees that you won't starve; if you are not yet hungry, then
waiting 99 turns will make you, at worst, hungry (but never weak or
starving).  Note that this is without anything being worn that increases
food consumption (rings, amulets, etc): even in those cases, I would
bet that waiting 99 turns while not hungry would make you at most weak
(ring of regeneration excepted).

BTW, I have tried waiting 9999 turns before, and have never starved:
what always happens is that I faint, and when I have woken up, the
waiting is no longer carried out.  If you are relatively safe (hah!)
from monster attacks, and you don't like typing, I think "9999." would
do the trick (not in vaults though: those pesky guards keep coming
along).

